{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1451376-house-tremere-reborn-ish","id":1451376,"title":"House Tremere Reborn...ish?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-08T13:36:13-07:00","id":1451376,"title":"House Tremere Reborn...ish?","content":"So I have recently started a new M20 game where the players are playing post Ascension/Apocalypse/Gehenna. I have lightly thumbed through the V5 SI, and with the Inner Council being wiped out, I began thinking if I were a former mage thaumaturgist of low generation, what type of contingency plans would I have in effect. Through middlemen and allies still with the Order of Hermes, a simulacrum to bring forth from their own genetic lineage, a new vessel... Long (back) story short, four players and four NPCs now have the Inner Council plus one unknown as their character's avatars.<br /> I know there are no hard logistics for it, since the embrace shatters the avatar, but I found it a nice gimmick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26882-siegetroll","name":"SiegeTroll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T04:31:19-07:00","id":1451428,"title":"","content":"Shatter isn't the same thing as destroy and can mean a lot of different things depending on what the Avatar actually is. Sounds reasonable to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T01:48:40-07:00","id":1451621,"title":"","content":"Since Tremere himself is a vampire via his own scheming, how could the House Tremere possibly be reborn? Houses aren't genetic, they are named after leaders, and Tremere is a disgraced traitor from a Mage perspective. Any human mages of his house would simply be Order of Hermes. Heck, a few probably DID escape his transformation of his house, and simply became absorbed into the other houses of the Order of Hermes a thousand years ago. But a rebirth of the house? I can't see any Hermetic even wanting that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T03:00:41-07:00","id":1451625,"title":"","content":"I'd see that those of House Guernicus would begin an investigation, bring in some of those from House Flambeau for support, and quiet possible see that the Avatars in question are corrupted and need to be dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T04:58:17-07:00","id":1451640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1451376-house-tremere-reborn-ish?p=1451621#post1451621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Tremere himself is a vampire via his own scheming, how could the House Tremere possibly be reborn? Houses aren't genetic, they are named after leaders, and Tremere is a disgraced traitor from a Mage perspective. Any human mages of his house would simply be Order of Hermes. Heck, a few probably DID escape his transformation of his house, and simply became absorbed into the other houses of the Order of Hermes a thousand years ago. But a rebirth of the house? I can't see any Hermetic even wanting that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> A House it's a social structure so the means should be political/ideological. Such an attempt should involve titanic feats of politics (and also of magic to back them up)<br /> <br /> Unlikely ways I could see this happening:<br /> a) Tremere himself found a way to become human again and restore his True Magick. Bad blood still exists, but he promises to bring enough power &amp; knowledge to the Order that the pragmatic within could be persuaded to allow the House back<br /> <br /> b) The Order of Hermes decides to accept vampires in their midst. While this flies in the face of the history of the Order (and violates a tenet of the Code - punishable with death), I think it's also something that was being planned by a House Tytalus Master in Doissetep (a ghoul mage, died in the explosion) before the 2nd massa war. If things had worked differently, it might not be quite as impossible as one would think (still top tier hard).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:20:52-07:00","id":1451701,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that whether or not the Avatar of a Mage-turned-Vampire is actually shattered is one of those things that varies between sources and editions, and I don't know if there was ever a definitive answer given on the matter.<br /> <br /> The tricky part with what's proposed here is how difficult it is supposed to be to pull off. &quot;The Red Sign&quot; is a sourcebook discussing a potential ritual for using True Magic to remove the Curse of Caine and restore a vampire to life. IIRC, it's an extremely difficult feat for Mages even, which I would expect to mean a significantly more difficult task for a group of Thaumaturges. If there was going to be any Cainites that could do it, the Council of Seven and/or Tremere would be among the most likely candidates. It also depends on how seriously you take the story conceits of VtM in a M20 game; if you take VtM's lore seriously, the difficulty of the task is described as &quot;trying to roll more successes than God&quot; IIRC. Whereas if you're playing from a more Mage-centric perspective, then how difficult or easy such a task might be would be more a matter of Storyteller decision.<br /> <br /> One possible thing to look into is in the V20 book on the True Black Hand/Tal'Mahe'Ra; I can't remember the name for it, but there is a ritual in there for granting a vampire access to the Avatar of a ghouled Mage. Something like that might be an explanation for how the Council of Seven pulled it off. It might also provide an explanation for how they did it even if you believe their original Avatars were permanently destroyed; the Avatars your cabal of players have aren't their original Avatars, but instead ones that the Council warped and possessed.<br /> <br /> Assuming that Tremere himself is not as dedicated to his vampiric existence as some sources indicate (Blood Treachery IIRC), pulling something like this off may have been the actual intent of the ritual he powered with the deaths of the Tremere antitribu. Restoring some of the Council of Seven to try and reconstruct his powerbase among the Awakened might make sense in that context.<br /> <br /> I think there is actually a tiny faction of former House Tremere that still exists among the Order of Hermes; I think they may be mentioned in the &quot;Red Sign&quot;, but I can't remember for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}